<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Shared container so the home-screen widget (and, later, the
         watch) can read the forecast snapshot the app writes. Must be
         registered on the Apple Developer portal + enabled on the App ID
         for signed / TestFlight / App Store builds. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.com.taxottic.app</string>
    </array>
    <!-- Push Notifications (APNs). @capacitor/push-notifications registers
         with APNs directly on iOS (no Firebase on this target, the app is
         SPM-based with no GoogleService-Info.plist), so register() returns a
         raw APNs device token that CapacitorNativeInit POSTs to
         /api/push/register as platform:"ios".
         MUST BE `production`. The previous value was `development`, on the
         belief that "a distribution build's provisioning profile promotes
         this to production automatically at archive time".

         THAT BELIEF IS FALSE, and production data disproves it. Build 40
         (1.3.11, a TestFlight distribution build) reported, 64 times:

           status : registration_error
           detail : no valid "aps-environment" entitlement string found
                    for application

         in push_registration_state, while Android and web both read
         `registered`. The signed binary carried `development`, APNs
         rejects that on a distribution build, and iOS therefore produced
         ZERO device_tokens rows since the feature shipped in July.

         Xcode does not rewrite this key. The archive is signed with
         whatever the file says.

         COST OF THE OTHER DIRECTION: a locally-built Debug app on a
         tethered device now gets a production APNs entitlement, so a dev
         push token will not work against the sandbox. That is the right
         trade here: every device that matters (testers, the store) runs a
         distribution build, and nobody on this project debugs push over a
         cable. If that changes, split CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS per build
         configuration rather than reverting this value.
         REQUIRES: the "Push Notifications" capability enabled on the
         com.taxottic.app App ID in the Apple Developer portal, otherwise
         signing fails with "provisioning profile doesn't include the
         aps-environment entitlement". Same portal-side step the
         application-groups entitlement above needed. -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
